Before Running main code please do the following steps to set up the PGAdmin database required for the app to function

Step 1:

Please download and install PostgreSQL software. Below is a link to PostgresSQL websight where you can download the
software form

Link: https://www.postgresql.org/download/

Step 2:

Once installed please Open op pgAdmin4 and log in to Your preferred Server.

next please Right click on databases and select Create -> Database.

enter cleaning_inventory_db as the databasename.

click the save button

Step 3:

Right click on the newly made database and select Query Tool
click Open file and Brows for the file Schema.SQL supplied in the zip file under the database folder (src -> main -> java -> database).

Open the file and click the Execute button or press F5

Wait until the "Query returned successfully" appears.

Step 4:

Edit the DBConnecton.java file by entering the User details and password and URL if you have saved it under a different
name.


Below is a link to our Git hub repository 

Link: https://github.com/steven-raian-piek/UniversityCleaningInventorySystem

